{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy","id":849461,"title":"Chronicles of Darkness Mummy?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-18T14:43:24-07:00","id":849461,"title":"Chronicles of Darkness Mummy?","content":"Has anything been announced about Chronicles of Darkness Mummy/Mummy 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1187-prons","name":"Prons","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1187_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T15:00:21-07:00","id":849470,"title":"","content":"We still gotta get Geist announced.<br /> <br /> One can reasonably assume that a Mummy 2nd is somewhere down the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T15:01:04-07:00","id":849471,"title":"","content":"Mage, Promethean, Changeling, and Hunter all need to come out first. Then we have to see if Geist is getting a new edition or not. /Then/ we might get Mummy.<br /> <br /> I don't like to admit it, but it'll be another two or three years before Mummy 2e if things continue at the current rate. I can only hope we get supplements to ease the pain in the time until then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 03-18-2016, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T15:09:07-07:00","id":849474,"title":"","content":"I'ma gonna lay this down.<br /> <br /> It's not a question of <i>if</i> Geist is getting a Second Edition. It absolutely is. The question is <i>when</i>.<br /> <br /> The same is largely true for Mummy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T15:35:40-07:00","id":849482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=849474#post849474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'ma gonna lay this down.<br /> <br /> It's not a question of <i>if</i> Geist is getting a Second Edition. It absolutely is. The question is <i>when</i>.<br /> <br /> The same is largely true for Mummy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Geist 2e shows up every single time someone ends up talking about what new books they want. OPP knows that the demand for it is there, and they actually have a fairly free hand to do what they want with it, since there has been so little written about Geist. I'd fully expect that we can start speculation about Mummy once that's happened. <br /> <br /> As and aside - Arc, I <b>knew</b> that was going to end up as your avatar before they day was out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T11:33:35-07:00","id":849814,"title":"","content":"Good to hear. So, in the meantime let's do a little roleplaying. Onyx has contracted YOU to write the main book for Mummy 2.0. What do you want to add to the new edition? What specific God-Machine modifications would you make to traits like vice and virtues and Memory? What would you take away?<br /> <br /> For my part I feel like the Egyptian theme has been perfectly explored through this edition. I'd like to see more multiculturalism- though I have hopes Rio will satisfy some of that urge anyway. More information on the 42 Judges and their cults would be good. Fill in the ranks of the Lifeless with underworld demons abominations in the spirit of the Cthonic Entity and other lovecraftian horrors. If there's a way to make ghosts and the underworld a more active part/concern for the Arisen without stealing Geist's thunder, I say use it. <br /> <br /> Perhaps provide a Mummy more opportunities to prolong the Descent? Like, if a Mummy actively aids another Arisen in their Purpose (and their Judge approves) or thwarts the Purpose of another Mummy (and their Judge approves!), including the goals of a local Nome or Guild? Maybe scale it so that a very high Sekhem Mummy has almost no opportunities to preserve their Sekhem while a mid to low Sekhem Mummy has increasingly more options available?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T12:02:16-07:00","id":849823,"title":"","content":"Mummy has some of my favorite fluff, so I would probably change exactly none of it (only expand things 1e hasn't detailed or explored much) and just clean up mechanics. Maybe tidy up the presentation a bit, though I still think the Player/Storyteller division in the core works very well for the kind of game Mummy is.<br /> <br /> Decree is a fairly vestigial x-splat all things considered and could be made more distinct - or just removed. The Mummy template should probably get a power boost to bring some of its original strengths in line with 2e. Pillar attribute boosting has always been needlessly complicated and could use being simplified and made more reliable. I'd also rework the structure of Utterances, as to avoid the annoyingly repeated instances of going back and adjusting Pillar distribution during character creation to make sure you could actually use all three tiers of your chosen spells and didn't end up with fillers.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how I'd change or adjust the progression of the Descent, but there are a lot of interesting suggestions and additions floating around 2e hacks to consider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-19-2016, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T12:14:37-07:00","id":849830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=849823#post849823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'd also rework the structure of Utterances, as to avoid the annoyingly repeated instances of going back and adjusting Pillar distribution during character creation to make sure you could actually use all three tiers of your chosen spells and didn't end up with fillers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Easiest thing I can think of in line with the current development trends is to have them operate like Changeling Contracts in 2E - They have a base benefit that can be modified if you meet the Pillar Pre-Req. So an Utterance that requires Ba 5 now might still work if you don't have Ba 5, but once you get it, you have access to that modification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T12:26:43-07:00","id":849836,"title":"","content":"I've been contracted to handle Mummy 2?<br /> <br /> I see if David Hill wants it.<br /> <br /> And no to the multiculturalism. The mythology of Irem and the history of the Arisen is strong, good, potent stuff. I would not dare take away some of the greatest power this game has by saying &quot;And now, the Nameless Empire that was founded in Brazil&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T12:54:25-07:00","id":849847,"title":"","content":"Definitely keep Mummy firmly Iremite/Egyptian. M:tR exists if you're desperate for Chinese mummies and becoming Twice-Arisen doesn't satisfy you.<br /> <br /> Expand the Decree into something meaningful beyond just your choice of Judge and defining Pillar. Add in that unique form of Sybaris from Ruins of Empire as a default option, and turn Sybaris into a chain of Conditions. Give rules for building your own Slaughterers and other demons, so that the Arisen have foes other than Amkhat and themselves to fight. Cults and Pyramid play get an entire chapter to themselves. Add in something similar to Monuments or my previously discussed Flashpoints, some sort of Touchstone-equivalent firmly rooted in your personal history. Toss in a list of easy to assemble Egyptian name parts. Players don't like doing that homework and I don't want Nephren-Ka and Imhotep at every table.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't change a damn thing, just add on. Mummy is alread a masterpiece in my eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T13:30:57-07:00","id":849851,"title":"","content":"Multiculturalism in the true meaning of the word would be a very poor choice for the themes and core of Mummy. It'd dillute very significant and unique qualities of Irem and the Arisen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-19-2016, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T13:37:55-07:00","id":849855,"title":"","content":"Something I'd like to see would be some more clarification on Duat, the Underworld, Neter-Khertet, Twilight and the differences or lack thereof between them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T13:40:24-07:00","id":849856,"title":"","content":"More on Twilight/Neter-Kherter(same thing), sure.<br /> <br /> Duat and the Underworld? No. You're not going to play in Duat except for once, maybe twice, and you never go to the Underworld. Answering questions about the two, particularly in the light of never using them, cheapens the mystery of the game and the joy of players making up their own answers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T13:42:03-07:00","id":849857,"title":"","content":"What YOLF, Arc, and atamajakki are saying, basically. I would also like to de-emphasize Guilds as global, political entities and focus more on Mummies as isolated creatures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T13:45:38-07:00","id":849858,"title":"","content":"I have a whole train of thought on what Mummy 2 should have. Just, no time to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T13:45:45-07:00","id":849859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=849856#post849856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More on Twilight/Neter-Kherter(same thing), sure.<br /> <br /> Duat and the Underworld? No. You're not going to play in Duat except for once, maybe twice, and you never go to the Underworld. Answering questions about the two, particularly in the light of never using them, cheapens the mystery of the game and the joy of players making up their own answers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I meant in the Storyteller's part.<br /> <br /> For Twilight/Neter-Khertet I was always a little confused, seeing as it was always described like the Shadowlands from oWoD. As a kind of semi-separate world while Twilight was always described as a state of existence in the real world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T13:55:53-07:00","id":849865,"title":"","content":"I would simplify character creation. The mix of attributes, skills, and pillars required for utterances and affinities makes effective character generation confusing to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T14:02:27-07:00","id":849867,"title":"","content":"I still wouldn't explain it in the Storyteller's section. Duat and the Underworld's relaiton to one another should basically just never addressed. It's not important, and it's more fun to speculate on than answer.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, as much I loved the noble experiment, I'd get rid of the 'Storyteller's Wall&quot; in regards to the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T14:05:07-07:00","id":849869,"title":"","content":"To be entirely honest, there's not much point to it if everyone enthralled by the book is just going to be read both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T14:07:19-07:00","id":849870,"title":"","content":"In this era of people looking up shit online, there aren't secrets anymore.<br /> <br /> Honestly, Mummy did it better with the hiding the truth in various books that you then have to string together. The majority of the work is between Dreams and Deceived, but the whole picture thing from pieces worked great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T14:20:22-07:00","id":849873,"title":"","content":"That's true. I regularly go back and read parts of the core, Deceived and now Dreams together to get a more coherent picture of the whole or refresh my understanding. Sometimes I find links I missed before and take new conclusions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T14:27:45-07:00","id":849875,"title":"","content":"When MtC came out, a new Sothic Turn had just happened; so we had a flood of Arisen\u2026 arising, all at once. That was deliberate. But in 2e, we'll be in the aftermath of that great confluence, unless 2e revises the calendar established in 1e and pushes the mass-arising back. I'd rather it not, myself; you just can't keep pushing it back year after year, as it will eventually start getting ridiculous. So what I'd like to see in 2e is for its base assumptions to be recalibrated for a world where most or all of the Arisen have finished their Sothic Turn Descents, and those Arisen who are being featured in the chronicle are mainly ones who have started new Descents due to meddling on this side (whether it be \u201cyour cult needs you\u201d or \u201cgrave robbers have disturbed your tomb\u201d). Pyramid-style play becomes a big deal when the number of Arisen who are still up and about dwindles, and teams of Arisen become increasingly improbable. <br /> <br /> So in 2e, I want more focus on cultists as player characters. <br /> <br /> For the first time in the nWoD/ChroD, introduce <i>just a touch</i> of metaplot: the Heretic has succeeded in getting <i>Dreams of Avarice</i> widely distributed, and Apotheosis is now a known quantity that he is not alone in achieving. The Deathless who are free of the Judges are still few and far between, and still mostly rumors; but there are now cults who are calling their founders back with the express purpose of seeking Apotheosis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T14:33:29-07:00","id":849877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=849875#post849875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But in 2e, we'll be in the aftermath of that great confluence, unless 2e revises the calendar established in 1e and pushes the mass-arising back.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was already a window of a century or two whose midpoint is that Sothic Turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T14:34:05-07:00","id":849878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=849847#post849847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely keep Mummy firmly Iremite/Egyptian. M:tR exists if you're desperate for Chinese mummies and becoming Twice-Arisen doesn't satisfy you.<br /> <br /> Expand the Decree into something meaningful beyond just your choice of Judge and defining Pillar. Add in that unique form of Sybaris from Ruins of Empire as a default option, and turn Sybaris into a chain of Conditions. Give rules for building your own Slaughterers and other demons, so that the Arisen have foes other than Amkhat and themselves to fight. Cults and Pyramid play get an entire chapter to themselves. Add in something similar to Monuments or my previously discussed Flashpoints, some sort of Touchstone-equivalent firmly rooted in your personal history. Toss in a list of easy to assemble Egyptian name parts. Players don't like doing that homework and I don't want Nephren-Ka and Imhotep at every table.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't change a damn thing, just add on. Mummy is alread a masterpiece in my eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I just want to thank you for directing me to Ruins of Empire. I hadn't read that section of the Dark Eras spoilers until now, and I absolutely love the Mummy Merits there and the whole idea of Enticement Sybaris.<br /> <br /> On my own end, I agree that more Lifeless monstrosities (from Duat or otherwise) would be great. Personally, I want a bit more information on the Twice-Arisen. What are they like? Are their Memories permanently confused, or do they eventually solidify their original Iremite identity? Considering the Deceived can undergo the ritual as frequently as they desire, and the Shuankhsen default to incarnating in a stolen body, a bit about the Twice-Arisen experience would be great.<br /> <br /> Also- mechanical descriptions of Apotheosis and/or making Relics. Some details on how an Ascended Mummy returns from <i>henet </i>would be awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 03-19-2016, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T16:20:01-07:00","id":849920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=849877#post849877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was already a window of a century or two whose midpoint is that Sothic Turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, whenever 2e happens, we'll still be in the middle of the Great Arising. From Sothis Ascends, it sounds like Mummies that are smart can stay functional for decades into a Turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T16:22:52-07:00","id":849921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=849877#post849877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was already a window of a century or two whose midpoint is that Sothic Turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Arisen don't all arise at once come the year of the Sothic Turn, but each do so when that amount of time passes after their last Sothic rising.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T16:23:44-07:00","id":849923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=849869#post849869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be entirely honest, there's not much point to it if everyone enthralled by the book is just going to be read both.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=849870#post849870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this era of people looking up shit online, there aren't secrets anymore.<br /> <br /> Honestly, Mummy did it better with the hiding the truth in various books that you then have to string together. The majority of the work is between Dreams and Deceived, but the whole picture thing from pieces worked great.</div> </div> </div> </div>I managed to run a campaign for more than a year without the players looking up the answers online or reading the Storyteller section of the book. So speaking from practice, that part actually worked as intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T16:28:27-07:00","id":849925,"title":"","content":"You're one group.<br /> <br /> Out of a great deal more that just said &quot;Fuck it&quot; and read it anyways.<br /> <br /> Next.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T17:58:06-07:00","id":849942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=849875#post849875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the first time in the nWoD/ChroD, introduce <i>just a touch</i> of metaplot: the Heretic has succeeded in getting <i>Dreams of Avarice</i> widely distributed, and Apotheosis is now a known quantity that he is not alone in achieving. The Deathless who are free of the Judges are still few and far between, and still mostly rumors; but there are now cults who are calling their founders back with the express purpose of seeking Apotheosis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good god no. I'm tired enough as it is of fending off people who think Mummy has a metaplot; don't prove them right. It undermines a core concept of the CofD as a whole.<br /> <br /> And besides, I doubt the Heretic is going to reach more mummies in the last four years than he has in the last 5000. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=849878#post849878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I want a bit more information on the Twice-Arisen. What are they like? Are their Memories permanently confused, or do they eventually solidify their original Iremite identity? Considering the Deceived can undergo the ritual as frequently as they desire, and the Shuankhsen default to incarnating in a stolen body, a bit about the Twice-Arisen experience would be great.<br /> <br /> Also- mechanical descriptions of Apotheosis and/or making Relics. Some details on how an Ascended Mummy returns from <i>henet </i>would be awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understood the Twice-Arisen as having very little confusion as to their identities. The process is largely there to impart modern skills and a new face; I can't imagine much of the memory/identity/soul of the original occupant is there to trouble you. Clarification would be nice, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=849920#post849920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, whenever 2e happens, we'll still be in the middle of the Great Arising. From Sothis Ascends, it sounds like Mummies that are smart can stay functional for decades into a Turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sothic Turn isn't one year, but rather the start of a span in which the Arisen start to come to. While those who underwent the Rite earliest woke up in 2012, we'll likely have more Descents starting probably until 2026 at the earliest; I'm sure the ritual sacrifice of an entire civilization wasn't exactly a speedy process, especially if it was as thorough as Book of the Deceived made it out to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T18:46:28-07:00","id":849957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=849925#post849925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're one group.<br /> <br /> Out of a great deal more that just said &quot;Fuck it&quot; and read it anyways.<br /> <br /> Next.</div> </div> </div> </div>So by that I can assume you have the numbers? Because the nature of a forum like this means that anecdotal evidence is always likely to skew towards those who have read the books in detail, which may or may not be representative of actual player groups. Only one of the six players I've run through Mummy are on this forum, for example.<br /> <br /> Besides, it's not like the wall actually hurt anyone. From my perspective it was nice to have a clear division of &quot;knowledge characters are expected to know&quot; and &quot;knowledge characters will likely need to rediscover by examining their memories&quot;. While I mostly preferred to examine events in different time periods featuring the character as a Mummy, it was cool to have a few facts to toss around about the characters' mortal days that they were not initially aware of for those rare flashbacks to Irem. And if your group have all read Mummy cover to cover and would just roll their eyes at such a &quot;revelation&quot; in-game, that's fine. Don't make those revelations and treat them as assumed knowledge. That's what you'd be doing if you didn't have the wall, but its existence gives an added option to those whose groups don't choose to &quot;fuck it&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T19:13:41-07:00","id":849963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=849957#post849957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So by that I can assume you have the numbers? Because the nature of a forum like this means that anecdotal evidence is always likely to skew towards those who have read the books in detail, which may or may not be representative of actual player groups. Only one of the six players I've run through Mummy are on this forum, for example.<br /> <br /> Besides, it's not like the wall actually hurt anyone. From my perspective it was nice to have a clear division of &amp;quot;knowledge characters are expected to know&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;knowledge characters will likely need to rediscover by examining their memories&amp;quot;. While I mostly preferred to examine events in different time periods featuring the character as a Mummy, it was cool to have a few facts to toss around about the characters' mortal days that they were not initially aware of for those rare flashbacks to Irem. And if your group have all read Mummy cover to cover and would just roll their eyes at such a &amp;quot;revelation&amp;quot; in-game, that's fine. Don't make those revelations and treat them as assumed knowledge. That's what you'd be doing if you didn't have the wall, but its existence gives an added option to those whose groups don't choose to &amp;quot;fuck it&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with you on this. Not every product needs to be bifurcated, but it can add something for those people who want to stay in the dark, and is at worst a minor obstacle for those who don't. For something like the core rulebook, it certainly seems reasonable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T20:20:39-07:00","id":849988,"title":"","content":"Before responding, Apologies for being curt. I had to run and speak fast.<br /> <br /> That said, I've been on these forums since their inception(as have been a great number of people, I know, and I've seen so many people just steam roll ahead. It's now at a point where we don't even <i>bother</i> with spoiler threads anymore. Several reviews have cited how hiding things in a Storyteller's Section doesn't work anymore.<br /> <br /> Quite frankly, we live in an age of transparency, at least in this neck of the woods. Trying to hide things hasn't worked out great.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying don't have the secrets in the Storyteller's Chapter(not Section), but I am saying that the idea of the wall doesn't work, and 2E might be better served dismissing it. This is an opinion, mind. I just don't think it ever really worked on a large scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T23:03:29-07:00","id":850041,"title":"","content":"I think if they had marketed it a little bit better, where they by default split the core into player and ST books and then offered the full version as a separate thing, maybe the split could have worked better? That would have made the Deluxe Kickstarter somewhat more difficult.<br /> <br /> I don't know, there are plenty of books that have a small section right in the back that's full of GM only stuff that's usually respected but they usually aren't half the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T23:16:16-07:00","id":850042,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's the years of Cthulhu gaming in me, but is it really so hard to say &quot;you know this but your character doesn't?&quot; Trust your players to not metagame instead of acting like they won't read ahead.<br /> <br /> Unraveling &quot;what were the Shan'iatu really up to&quot; is way less interesting than &quot;why the hell did I butcher my Viking cult (and how did I get here, anyway?)&quot; over the course of play. Personal revelations are much more fun than cosmic ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 03-20-2016, 02:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T23:19:01-07:00","id":850043,"title":"","content":"I for one as a Storyteller almost always assume my players have read the storyteller section and plan accordingly. With the vast resources available on the internet, maintaining the wall of secrecy is time consuming and wastes space that could be better served with content.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T00:51:58-07:00","id":850052,"title":"","content":"Well, I usually can't get my players to even read the players sections of the books, so I'm fairly confident that the GM stuff is safe!<br /> <br /> But yeah, really when I think of a book that I think did it rather well, Eclipse Phase comes to mind. It lays out a lot of interesting questions in the book and in the last chapter they reveal some of the answers to the mysteries they've put forward. Not a lot of wordcount spent, and the mysteries, while big, aren't going to alter day-to-day stuff in the game but it's nice to have concrete answers and if the GM decides to play with it, well, it's there. And I -do- think that there's a genuine sort of thrill you get from learning something new both as a player and a character, although I think a lot of people overvalue that thrill - a lot of horror stories or extreme complications can form trying to jump through hoops instead of just telling it out straight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T02:31:29-07:00","id":850065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=849988#post849988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before responding, Apologies for being curt. I had to run and speak fast.<br /> <br /> That said, I've been on these forums since their inception(as have been a great number of people, I know, and I've seen so many people just steam roll ahead. It's now at a point where we don't even <i>bother</i> with spoiler threads anymore. Several reviews have cited how hiding things in a Storyteller's Section doesn't work anymore.<br /> <br /> Quite frankly, we live in an age of transparency, at least in this neck of the woods. Trying to hide things hasn't worked out great.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;This neck of the woods&quot; is the key, I think. Of course telegraphing spoilers here, on this forum, is pointless. You can safely assume that anyone on this forum is an avid fan of Onyx Path in some capacity. Heck, a lot of us here even even read books we don't intend to ever run. But for a lot of gamers out there, the game is to be approached like, well, a game. The book only enters the equation after the group has decided on their next game, and then you read only what you need to play the game. Why would you read the Storyteller section of Mummy if you don't intend to run Mummy? That defeats the premise of the game you've agreed to play in. That would be silly. To anyone approaching the game as a game, reading a book for &quot;the experience&quot;, the answers, or just pure joy in the writing seems pointless. The game is there to be played and you don't start off by breaking the rules.<br /> <br /> The key is that a lot more people play Chronicles of Darkness than post on this forum. And the kind of people who do post on this forum are, almost by virtue of doing so, approaching the game lines with a different mentality to the players who do not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=849988#post849988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying don't have the secrets in the Storyteller's Chapter(not Section), but I am saying that the idea of the wall doesn't work, and 2E might be better served dismissing it. This is an opinion, mind. I just don't think it ever really worked on a large scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>The wall is literally just one page and a short paragraph addressing the concept. And it did work in my game. I think it's a small price to pay to telegraph the intent, regardless of the success, when you're not even opposed to the concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T02:42:48-07:00","id":850069,"title":"","content":"As I've only forayed into the 2nd edition system briefly, having picked up Werewolf the Forsaken 2e. The only real mechanical change I'd like to see in a 2e version of Mummy is smoothing out the power curve and utility of different sorts of Utterances. There are across the game line some where a few levels of the power, either due to the scope or mechanics of the Utterance feel less than useful at least on paper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T03:30:52-07:00","id":850083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=850069#post850069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I've only forayed into the 2nd edition system briefly, having picked up Werewolf the Forsaken 2e. The only real mechanical change I'd like to see in a 2e version of Mummy is smoothing out the power curve and utility of different sorts of Utterances. There are across the game line some where a few levels of the power, either due to the scope or mechanics of the Utterance feel less than useful at least on paper.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, I actually have the opposite complaint with Utterances. They felt remarkably useful on a consistent fashion way beyond most abilities in either 1E or some 2E games (Demon, for example). There are literally only two Utterances I can think of where my group could see little use for. Seeds of Life and Waters of Life and Death.<br /> <br /> Which ones felt bad from your perspective?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T05:53:54-07:00","id":850102,"title":"","content":"On a slightly different tack, what locations would you choose to go in depth of for Mummy 2e? Right now I'd lean towards:<br /> <br /> - Khartoum, Sudan: The meeting point of the two Niles<br /> - Dar es Salam, Tanzania: still Africa, but not in Irem's original sphere of influence <br /> - Halifax, Canada: If there's anywhere in Canada that has cultists worshiping Lovecraftian entities, it is Halifax, and I say that with love<br /> - Honolulu, Hawaii: Having one location that's unintutive gives us a bit more variety and can create some interesting scenarios. Plus, that gives me an American setting that's totally different from anything else that's been done, <br /> - Havana, Cuba: A country formerly trapped in time and surrounded by enemies, now (finally) being able to loosen up a bit. Sound familiar? <br /> - Cilegon, Indonesia: Jakarta by Starlight was amazing, but I don't want to overwrite it. Cilegon is less well known, but could have just as much potential. <br /> - Lima, Peru: A city founded by conquistadors in one of the cradles of civilization? You know the Arisen would be all over that.<br /> - Wellington, New Zealand: We've seen Australia, now let's see its closest neighbour. Plus the idea that Weta Workshops may have produced some literal artifacts that are now kicking around the islands is hilarious. <br /> - Tokyo, Japan: Duh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T08:38:32-07:00","id":850135,"title":"","content":"Toronto, Canada? One of the Mesen-Nebu Guildmasters is set up there, and there's an established Changeling Freehold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T09:23:11-07:00","id":850149,"title":"","content":"I know they wouldn't include the first two to avoid treading old ground, but this was a list I made up a while ago:<ul><li>Washington DC</li> <li>Rio de Janeiro</li> <li>Tokyo</li> <li>Cairo</li> <li>Venice</li> </ul>Short and mostly unoriginal, but I feel like it covered the essentials","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T09:45:44-07:00","id":850158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=850135#post850135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Toronto, Canada? One of the Mesen-Nebu Guildmasters is set up there, and there's an established Changeling Freehold.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd go with Ottawa over TO if I had to take a city in Ontario. Close enough to be politically influenced, but it gives us a new location. Plus, taking the capital could mirror DC nicely, and the centennial flame looks like a project involving Sekhem if I ever saw one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T10:16:41-07:00","id":850174,"title":"","content":"Alexandra, Istanbul, and London all strike me as incredibly suitable Mummy settings due to how far back their individual histories stretch; I can't help but feel like any settings in the corebook should not only work for the modern day, but have suggestions for important moments in history to flashback to.<br /> <br /> Second Chances, you're knockong it out of the park with that Honolulu suggestion. I'm not sure why I like that so much.<br /> <br /> A Chinese setting might as well be mandatory; give the Arisen somewhere to deal with that has a history just as long as the Mediterranean, but with cultures and magics they're wholly unfamiliar with. Then slap on a dash of &quot;what does Communism mean to the Arisen, who are both slaves and slave-owners themselves&quot; and dazzle them with the rapid pace things have changed at in the last few decades. It would be a vibrant mix of themes and inspiration that feels too bad to miss, not the least of which because it gives you a chance to be a Twice-Arisen that looks like the bad guy from Big Trouble in Little China.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T11:09:50-07:00","id":850196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=850174#post850174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second Chances, you're knockong it out of the park with that Honolulu suggestion. I'm not sure why I like that so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Call it the James Jacobs principle. When James assigns domains for Gods in Pathfinder, he says he always tries to included one that makes people tilt there head and say &quot;huh, I wouldn't have expected that.&quot; That's basically what I did here, just with settings instead of domains. You aren't wrong about that something intangible thought. I feel like its because Hawaii is so isolated and has such a mix of different cultures that makes it unique. It just... fits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T14:12:39-07:00","id":850252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=850065#post850065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;This neck of the woods&quot; is the key, I think..</div> </div> </div> </div>This neck of the woods being RPG's, not Onyx Path Forums","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T15:19:24-07:00","id":850272,"title":"","content":"2E wish: don't make me read between the lines across multiple books to understand the game. Keep a storyteller only section, fine, just actually use it to explain the premise rather than doing half of it and making me go hunting for the rest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T15:37:49-07:00","id":850281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=850252#post850252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This neck of the woods being RPG's, not Onyx Path Forums</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I'd say you're wrong, at least locally. The fraction of regular players of RPGs in my area who actually use the internet with respect to their games is minute. Most treat it as a game to play with friends, not an international online community, and certainly don't go so far as to seek out spoilers for story elements online.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T15:48:45-07:00","id":850287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=850272#post850272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2E wish: don't make me read between the lines across multiple books to understand the game. Keep a storyteller only section, fine, just actually use it to explain the premise rather than doing half of it and making me go hunting for the rest.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a difference between understanding the premise and understanding all the mysteries inherent to it, and you really shouldn't need more than the Mummy core book for the former.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T15:48:59-07:00","id":850289,"title":"","content":"Well, that's the problem. I might be wrong locally, but considering the number of reviews and comments of folks on the net being our next best representation of the gaming community that concerns itself with Mummy on the whole, it would see I'm right. Problem is, we have no idea just how representative these folkies are. I assume they are quite representative, you seem to disagree.<br /> <br /> So, instead, I'm going to point out that while the truth is strewn through the books (and I do like that), the two main books that do the most for unveiling the truth are much more openly and convincingly GM's books, while the Core, Guildhalls, and Sothis's Storyteller Walls often hid stuff that was either not actually secretive or obstuse/sly enough that with the context of Deceived and Dreams, it could be hard to tell what the secret was.<br /> <br /> THere's <i>got</i> to be a better way to handle the secrets of Mummy than the Wall. I don't know if Storyteller books are the answer or not, but there's gotta be a better way to do it.<br /> <br /> Anyways, we're bogging the thread down-if it matters that much, we should make a separate thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T16:08:03-07:00","id":850293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=850289#post850289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that's the problem. I might be wrong locally, but considering the number of reviews and comments of folks on the net being our next best representation of the gaming community that concerns itself with Mummy on the whole, it would see I'm right. Problem is, we have no idea just how representative these folkies are. I assume they are quite representative, you seem to disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Locally I can name, personally, about a dozen RPG players (and I know for a fact that there a more, but I can't say with any certainty that those players have ever even heard of Mummy). I've personally run more than half of those players I do know through Mummy. Given the number of regular posters on this forum, I'd say the experiences of a whole eight to twelve players is a pretty significant chunk, and it wouldn't take too many local communities like mine to render the online community and reviewers in the minority. Just imagine this topic with even six more posters discussing experiences like mine. But of course they won't, because that's the point. To anyone whose primary engagement is through the online community groups like mine are just about invisible and would be completely invisible without at least one member like myself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=850289#post850289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, instead, I'm going to point out that while the truth is strewn through the books (and I do like that), the two main books that do the most for unveiling the truth are much more openly and convincingly GM's books, while the Core, Guildhalls, and Sothis's Storyteller Walls often hid stuff that was either not actually secretive or obstuse/sly enough that with the context of Deceived and Dreams, it could be hard to tell what the secret was.<br /> <br /> THere's <i>got</i> to be a better way to handle the secrets of Mummy than the Wall. I don't know if Storyteller books are the answer or not, but there's gotta be a better way to do it.<br /> <br /> Anyways, we're bogging the thread down-if it matters that much, we should make a separate thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I can totally agree that the Wall was not always <i>executed</i> well. A few of the revelations were certainly pretty tame and/or easily deduced, and there could easily be meatier stuff in there. The Core book itself did not actually have very many massive secrets (&quot;Oh, the strange and inhuman necromancers who founded the Empire were also responsible for destroying it? I never saw that coming!&quot;). Among my group I think &quot;Shuankhsen were created by the same process that fuelled the Rite&quot; was the biggest twist to come from the Core.<br /> <br /> But that said, I think Deceived actually mentioned at some point that it didn't have a Wall because, in a regular Mummy game, it was always going to be a Storyteller-only book. And in a Deceived game, yeah, the Temakh are going to make sure the Deceived are already going in with a great deal of knowledge. As for Dreams, I'd say that it should be a Storyteller only product as well, at least until the players encounter it in-game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T16:54:58-07:00","id":850320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=850196#post850196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Call it the James Jacobs principle. When James assigns domains for Gods in Pathfinder, he says he always tries to included one that makes people tilt there head and say &quot;huh, I wouldn't have expected that.&quot; That's basically what I did here, just with settings instead of domains. You aren't wrong about that something intangible thought. I feel like its because Hawaii is so isolated and has such a mix of different cultures that makes it unique. It just... fits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is pathfinder a rpg game too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T17:06:59-07:00","id":850325,"title":"","content":"Yes, it's based off of the 3.5 edition of D&amp;D. James is fantastic RPG designer. My pipe dream would to have OP's design team collaborate with Pathfinder's to rebuild Planescape from the ground up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T21:57:16-07:00","id":850424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=850289#post850289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways, we're bogging the thread down-if it matters that much, we should make a separate thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that it's a thread about second edition <b>Mummy</b> I don't see how saying that we want the game's setting information consolidated is out of place.<br /> <br /> I think <b>Book of the Deceived</b> was a great place for information on its given topic, but, for example, there could've been a little more about them in the <i>storyteller's section of the core rulebook</i> than, &quot;They're masters of true name magic (whatever that means) and are mysterious. Despite that this is the GM section, though, we're still not going to reveal any mysteries. Buy a future supplement for that.&quot;<br /> <br /> Beating a dead horse, I guess. It's my favorite game but its biggest issue was presentation of its amazing setting and mechanics","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T00:12:32-07:00","id":850444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=850325#post850325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it's based off of the 3.5 edition of D&amp;D. James is fantastic RPG designer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... he isn't as much a RPG designer. He make adventures and setting content primarily. The Paizo people who actually make the RPG are people like Jason Bulmahn, Mark Seifter, and previously Sean K Reynolds. I mean, James Jacobs used to do more RPG designer stuff back in the 3.5e days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T17:10:03-07:00","id":850866,"title":"","content":"Let me see if I can take a crack at my hypothetical ultimate setting list for Mummy 2E:<br /> <br /> <b>Cairo, Egypt</b><br /> Honestly, even though the Arisen have spread all over the world, I couldn't imagine leaving Egypt out of the setting chapter. The Cairo area has been a center of Egyptian civilization since there has been an Egypt, and it's continuing importance in the modern era is reflected in the fact that many Egyptians refer to it simply as <i>Ma\u1e63r, </i>the Egyptian Arabic word for Egypt itself.<br /> <br /> <b>Florence, Italy </b><br /> Both the Arisen and the Deceived have been present in what is now Tuscany since the early days of Etruscan civilization, and there are some who have never left. During the late middle ages and the Italian Renaissance, Florence seemingly had something to offer all of the Deathless, becoming a center of art, architecture, banking, engineering, literature, philosophy, theater, and occult thought. The centuries since have not always been kind to the city, but many Arisen remain, as do their eternal, half-remembered foes .<br /> <br /> <b>Istanbul, Turkey </b><br /> The center of Mediterranean civilization during the third Sothic Turn may find itself practically flooded with Arisen during the fourth, exacerbating tensions in the capital of a nation already experiencing troubled times.<br /> <br /> <b>Lagos, Nigeria</b><br /> It's the biggest city in Africa, and Sub-Saharan Africa never seems to get it's fair share of attention in fantasy fiction and games. Mummy is the game line that seems to have dealt with Africa the most, so it's only natural that a major African city outside of Egypt should show up in Mummy 2E. Lagos itself is well outside of the ancient Iremite cultural sphere, and offers a great opportunity to explore some of the diverse cultures of west Africa.<br /> <br /> <b>London, UK</b><br /> Sort of a follow-up to <i>Ruins of Empire</i>, Mummies could have a unique and interesting perspective on the troubled legacy of the British Empire and colonial Egyptology. The Tef-Aabhi may mourn the loss of yet another promising world-empire, while the Mesen-Nebu appreciate London's continuing importance as a center of global trade and finance.<br /> <br /> <b>Mexico City, Mexico</b><br /> Is this already a setting in one of the CofD books? If not, why not? There are great opportunities for cults adapting Iremite dogma to Mesoamerican trappings, and it could make a great setting for stories about the conflict between the ancient and the modern, and between democracy and authoritarianism.<br /> <br /> <b>Santa Clara Valley, California</b><br /> &quot;Silicon Valley&quot; is, in some ways, the antithesis of everything the Arisen stand for, priding itself on its culture of &quot;disruptive innovation&quot; and aggressively promoting the virtues of the new and the temporary over the stable and traditional. And yet, an increasing number of Arisen who have seen the value of modern information technology - as a tool of trade, scholarship, surveillance, or control - have been drawn to the birthplace of the internet age.<br /> <br /> <b>Xi'an, China</b><br /> Formerly Chang'an, an ancient capital of China, it was the most important starting point of the silk road, which brought a trickle of Awakened into China over the centuries. It's glories have faded since it was the largest and wealthiest city in the world, but in the last few decades it has re-emerged as a cultural and economic center, and has begun to grow into one of China's newest megacities.<br /> <br /> <b>Tokyo, Japan</b><br /> Because there's always a Tokyo chapter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 03-21-2016, 08:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T17:23:41-07:00","id":850873,"title":"","content":"One minor thing worth noting; while Cairo is fun and the first place to spring to mind when one thinks of Egypt, I would love to cover Alexandria for both being slightly less overdone and also hosting some of the fiercest fighting in the Anglo-Egyptian War during the 1880s.<br /> <br /> Unrelated topic, but what would you all want from a Tokyo setting for Mummy? I imagine the local Arisen community is very small and largely recently arrived, and the regional powers probably don't want them meddling in the area.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T21:27:13-07:00","id":850957,"title":"","content":"There might possibly be a connection between dragon shrines and tombs; perhaps the Arisen of Tokyo have a stronger connection to the Shadow than elsewhere, or at least have to deal with it more, similarly to the Uratha and the Tengu.<br /> <br /> The Hogotitsu (sorry) certainly have some interest in harnessing Sekhem for themselves.<br /> <br /> I'd say the Arisen <i>are</i> the regional powers, in a sense, and that other splats have little interest in them since they are so infrequently awake.<br /> <br /> Didn't a Guildmaster of the Priests in Japan get herself killed, though, according to <b>Guildhalls</b> fluff and the SAS?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T22:32:50-07:00","id":850971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=850957#post850957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There might possibly be a connection between dragon shrines and tombs; perhaps the Arisen of Tokyo have a stronger connection to the Shadow than elsewhere, or at least have to deal with it more, similarly to the Uratha and the Tengu.</div> </div> </div> </div>This brings to mind the nameless cult referred to as the Voyagers. From first time I read of them in Werewolf 2e, with their beliefs and powers of names and words, they sounded like a Deceived Cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T01:24:43-07:00","id":851020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=850957#post850957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't a Guildmaster of the Priests in Japan get herself killed, though, according to <b>Guildhalls</b> fluff and the SAS?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be Sacmis, High Prophetess of Tokyo; she's a Shuankhsen now, as a result of being devoured by another Shuankhsen after making rather unwise used of Four Jar Magic, which sort of burned out her canopic jars. I imagine that the Su-Menent will still be reeling from that one through the fourth Sothic Turn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=850971#post850971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This brings to mind the nameless cult referred to as the Voyagers. From first time I read of them in Werewolf 2e, with their beliefs and powers of names and words, they sounded like a Deceived Cult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, that could be an interesting twist. I think Tokyo would probably be a logical place for the Deceived to have something of a power base, given that they have a history of establishing their tombs in places far from major centers of the Arisen. They can also shed their original bodies and take new ones without the risk of becoming Shuankhsen, unlike the Arisen, which might have given them a distinct advantage during the Edo period, when the city that would be Tokyo took shape and the Shogunate sought to bar movement into and out of the country. <br /> <br /> Maybe the loss of Sacmis is just the latest in a long line of tragedies that have befallen the Arisen of Tokyo. Cults might run afoul of both criminal organizations and law enforcement agencies with disturbing regularity, while relics sometimes simply disappear and the Lifeless always seem to turn up at the worst possible moment. The engineer(s) of these calamities is a powerful deceived, or possibly a deceived Meret, who are better connected than any of the Arisen of the city and love nothing more than making members of the other Guilds miserable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T01:31:50-07:00","id":851022,"title":"","content":"It might be fun to have a handful of Arisen and Deceived who arrived in Japan long ago and have ancient cults (and may well be Twice-Arisen to better blend in) clashing with those mummies who have arrived since the 1800s. I imagine the Meiji period brought with it at least some Western cults looking to exploit Japanese magic and relics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T18:02:21-07:00","id":851483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=851020#post851020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the loss of Sacmis is just the latest in a long line of tragedies that have befallen the Arisen of Tokyo. Cults might run afoul of both criminal organizations and law enforcement agencies with disturbing regularity, while relics sometimes simply disappear and the Lifeless always seem to turn up at the worst possible moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do like the idea that the Arisen's history in Tokyo is one of loss, tragedy, and failure. Not that the other splats don't have their difficulties but at least they can manage. The Arisen just watch as everything slips through their desiccated fingers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T20:51:07-07:00","id":852217,"title":"","content":"A few thoughts as Mummy is my favorite 1e game. <br /> <br /> Regarding storyteller v global info. I'll put a name to the problem--metagaming. Knowing info your character doesn't. My typical solution to this is to allow the narrators to be unreliable ones. As storytellers simply don't be afraid to twist facts around to suit the needs of your stories. Be upfront with your players and they'll enjoy the process of unravelling the mystery of which of the book's facts are facts and which are fictions. Of course this doesn't suit troupes that take a dogmatic approach. But these are sandbox games.<br /> <br /> Regarding the multicultural factor. Agree that they shouldn't be Arisen. Don't agree that other mummified immortals shouldn't show up someplace like a STG. In sandbox settings it's always good to provide folks with tools for apple cart upsetting. The key to mystery play after all is ensuring that the players don't know for sure what's around the corner.<br /> <br /> Other than those 2 pence, I'm looking forward to seeing where Mummy 2e goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T14:53:07-07:00","id":853174,"title":"","content":"I've been giving some more thought to a Tokyo setting for mummy, and I figured I'd share an NPC idea I've been playing around with:<br /> <br /> <b>Nefer-Mehenu, Mistress of the Deceived</b><br /> <br /> Under the grounds of J\u014dkan-ji temple lies a hidden chamber, small and unadorned, just large enough to house a single occupant and a few personal effects. Even if the Arisen of Tokyo were aware of its existence, none would suspect that this modest vault is home to a being of great and terrible power: Nefer-Mehenu, Guildmistress of the Akhem-Urtu. Known to her loyal cultists as <i>Fudai Bosatsu</i>, &quot;the Deathless Bodhisattva,&quot; the Mistress of the Deceived is a bearer of the Philosopher's Temakh who espouses a creed that superficially resembles Esoteric Buddhism. She built her current cult among the prostitutes and entertainers of Edo's Yoshiwara district, who collected coin and secrets from those among the elite who came to slake their vices among the impoverished and reviled. Her followers gained access to the halls of power when wealthy patrons took them home as wives and concubines, and today her nameless sect stands at the center of a conspiracy with ties to many of Tokyo's most influential families. <br /> <br /> For her part, Nefer-Mehenu has only vague memories of a time before she came to dwell in Tokyo, but she believes that she originally came to this far-flung corner of the world seeking solitude and peace. So long as the stain of the Arisen continues to befoul her city, however, she knows that she will find no respite, for the fevered ravings of her Temakh claw ceaselessly at her mind, demanding ever grander and more terrible acts of vengeance against the slaves of its ancient betrayers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T17:59:25-07:00","id":853254,"title":"","content":"I love it.<br /> <br /> While not nearly so developed, I've had the idea for a Cult shared by two Deceived (one of the Dancer and one of the Keeper) who exist as a cruel parody of the Shaolin temple, espousing a creed of existence without thought that consists entirely of instinct and action. While it's a little more pulp than I prefer (evil kung fu master mummies are hard to handle seriously), they're what always comes to mind when I imagine any Asian setting for Mummy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T15:21:38-07:00","id":853706,"title":"","content":"Mummy 3 with Jet Li is a funner movie than people give it credit for being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T17:18:21-07:00","id":853752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=853254#post853254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love it.<br /> <br /> While not nearly so developed, I've had the idea for a Cult shared by two Deceived (one of the Dancer and one of the Keeper) who exist as a cruel parody of the Shaolin temple, espousing a creed of existence without thought that consists entirely of instinct and action. While it's a little more pulp than I prefer (evil kung fu master mummies are hard to handle seriously), they're what always comes to mind when I imagine any Asian setting for Mummy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the first things that comes to my mind when I think of Mummy in east Asia are, well, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buddhist_mummies\" target=\"_blank\">Buddhist mummies</a>, and particularly the practice of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sokushinbutsu\" target=\"_blank\">Sokushinbutsu</a> in Japan. The practice of self-mummification may actually have originated in India or China, and it seems almost tailor-made to be a cover for mummies with (at least superficially) Buddhist cults in any of those regions. Actually, Buddhism is, in some ways, a great foundation for mummy cults.<br /> <br /> Buddhism encompasses a lot of very diverse sects with widely divergent beliefs, some of them quite small and obscure, and mummy cults could potentially find places to thrive within that complex framework. In most cases, the core of a Buddhist school consists of monks, whose at least partially cloistered existence could lend itself to secret rituals and hidden treasures. The basic philosophy of Buddhism emphasizes the role of suffering in human existence, and prescribes a path of right behavior by which one can escape from it, which could be made to align with the Law of the Judges. While Buddhism isn't necessarily theistic in and of itself, many schools of Buddhism describe a sometimes bewildering array of bodhisattvas, deities, demons, and other supernatural beings that could be identified with the Judges and other figures in Iremite theology. Likewise, the &quot;Pure Lands&quot; and heavens (or hells) described in some schools of Buddhism could easily be equated with Duat or A'aru by the Arisen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T17:24:30-07:00","id":853757,"title":"","content":"A Chinese Mummy chronicle could just as easily swing between ancient (likely Tribal) Cults rooted in particular families/schools/monasteries contrasted with those (Conspiracy and Enterprise) Cults that are based in modern business and crime, or else came over with the British in the last few hundred years.<br /> <br /> I have to wonder how many Relics were lost in the Cultural Revolution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T11:15:59-07:00","id":854562,"title":"","content":"On kind of a different tack: what's the theme antagonist of a hypothetical Mummy 2e? If any. I'd vote for the Deceived, but you could also have something more existential like Fallen World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T11:39:19-07:00","id":854569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=854562#post854562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On kind of a different tack: what's the theme antagonist of a hypothetical Mummy 2e? If any. I'd vote for the Deceived, but you could also have something more existential like Fallen World.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that Mage and Promethean didn't use antagonists for their spotlights whatsoever. I'd sooner see The Apotheosis Chronicle than The Deceived Chronicle, and even then I feel like the average Mummy game probably doesn't involve Apotheosis whatsoever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T12:46:31-07:00","id":854612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=854569#post854569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Keep in mind that Mage and Promethean didn't use antagonists for their spotlights whatsoever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes, that's why I mentioned Fallen World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T14:53:57-07:00","id":854687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=854569#post854569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Keep in mind that Mage and Promethean didn't use antagonists for their spotlights whatsoever. I'd sooner see The Apotheosis Chronicle than The Deceived Chronicle, and even then I feel like the average Mummy game probably doesn't involve Apotheosis whatsoever.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Of the two, Apotheosis sounds more game-changing than the Deceived (who you can play as, technically). Yes, many Mummy Chronicles don't deal with Apotheosis. But not all Vampire games deal with Strix, or Werewolf games with Idigam, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T15:42:42-07:00","id":854697,"title":"","content":"The material that's been published so far makes Apotheosis a pretty big deal in the setting, driving a lot of conflict and intrigue. Even if the PCs aren't seeking Apotheosis, there's a good chance that it will come up at some point in a chronicle, if only as a hot button issue in mummy politics or a heresy of which one might be suspected. It seems like at least as good a theme as the Strix or the Idigam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T16:16:10-07:00","id":854719,"title":"","content":"Not to mention the SAS is already called the Avarice chronicles, right? The politics around the book, apotheosis, the Heretic, the divide between tradition and change, the nagging doubts all mummies have about their service to the Judges, the truth about the cosmos and Shan'iatu. All of that could be expanded from just an adventure to full blown storytelling shenanigans and twists. Anyone who's read Dreams already knows its quite a revelation in theory, but not a shocking one. Finding ways to make players slowly get their feet we, starting with hints and horrors, culminating in Apotheosis and facing your Judge for the last time and finding A'aru... Id LOVE that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T19:02:44-07:00","id":854800,"title":"","content":"The Strix might not show up in every Vampire chronicle, but they point to both the internal struggle with the Beast that every one of the Kindred struggles with and provide one of the many reasons that the Danse Macabre is so full of mistrust, paranoia, and backstabbing. Not every Changeling is likely to cross paths with one of the Huntsmen, but all of them live in fear of being dragged back to Arcadia and shape their lives accordingly.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that the average Arisen either thinks the Lost Guild are long dead or tell themselves that their secrets have been lost to time; we as players didn't even know about them until three books into the line. <br /> <br /> Apotheosis, meanwhile, ties into the core conflict of Memory that informs every single Mummy chronicle. Even if your meret never crosses paths with the Heretic or never finds a copy of Dreams of Avarice, they still have to contend with their nature as powerful slaves who have lost much of their identity; Apotheosis is a neat way of encompassing everything core to Mummy on a thematic level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T02:20:22-07:00","id":854942,"title":"","content":"The Sothic Chronicles.<br /> <br /> Supernatural occurrences are typical in any age, but the Sothic Turns are like a flood compared to a high tide. For beings that literally predate history, how does this fourth Turning challenge them in ways new and unexpected? In an era more socially and technologically connected than ever, when mortals connect to those on the other side of the world, threats are everywhere. For the Arisen it's a time of loss as man turns his back on traditional mysticism, but for their enemies it's a time of <i>more</i>: the Shuankhsen feed <i>more</i>, the Deceived re-unite with each other <i>more</i>, amkhata pierce the veil <i>more</i>.<br /> <br /> The fears of Y2K didn't end. Mortals dream, and the brooding fear of the end of the world lurks in all their hearts...<br /> <br /> <i>more</i>.<br /> <br /> Strix rock the boat of the Damned's carefully balanced politics. Idigam are the unknowable prey to the world's best hunters. The Fallen World is an endless mystery to the only people who see the truth. The Sothic Turn is a period where those who have the longest memories are blindsided by a world that's outgrown them and changed in ways they didn't expect; it's time to either get busy livin' or get busy dyin', and that's a whole lot said for Mummies","signature":"","edited":{"userid":638,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","user":"reseru","date":".  added comparison to other lines 03-29-2016, 05:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T02:45:02-07:00","id":854950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=854942#post854942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sothic Chronicles.<br /> <br /> Supernatural occurrences are typical in any age, but the Sothic Turns are like a flood compared to a high tide. For beings that literally predate history, how does this fourth Turning challenge them in ways new and unexpected? In an era more socially and technologically connected than ever, when mortals connect to those on the other side of the world, threats are everywhere. For the Arisen it's a time of loss as man turns his back on traditional mysticism, but for their enemies it's a time of <i>more</i>: the Shuankhsen feed <i>more</i>, the Deceived re-unite with each other <i>more</i>, amkhata pierce the veil <i>more</i>.<br /> <br /> The fears of Y2K didn't end. Mortals dream, and the brooding fear of the end of the world lurks in all their hearts...<br /> <br /> <i>more</i>.<br /> <br /> Strix rock the boat of the Damned's carefully balanced politics. Idigam are the unknowable prey to the world's best hunters. The Fallen World is an endless mystery to the only people who see the truth. The Sothic Turn is a period where those who have the longest memories are blindsided by a world that's outgrown them and changed in ways they didn't expect; it's time to either get busy livin' or get busy dyin', and that's a whole lot said for Mummies</div> </div> </div> </div>Bonus points if the prior Turns serve as primary examples for an expanded focus on flashbacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T03:20:44-07:00","id":854965,"title":"","content":"One thing I'd like in the 2e, if it keeps storyteller/player divide. I liked the idea that from almost turn 2 until Napoleon and Ruins of Empire, mummies hadn't really a good idea where they were from. They remembered the River, but.. with Memory 3, a lot more should be hidden from Players. They shouldn think of Guilds directly as the job you had in Irem--its the mystic Guild that gives you purpose. I don't want my players saying &quot;I was a banker in Irem&quot; until their memory is high enough. Similarly, a LOT of back story of Irem could be hidden from players. I wouldn't mind a starter mummy thinking Irem was in china, only to find out (through memory) that they are second arisen, or a truly wild and rare thing (a slave traded from china to irem who got into a guild somehow). I would rather them see Guilds as mummy archetypes (rich and powerful, memory keeper, plain immortal, lovecraftian cultist, forward thinker) rather than Jobs right away. I'd also like to see a bit more on &quot;starter&quot; mummies--knowing only the basics of your character sheet, plus a little back story from your last descent, while leaving the rest of it alone. Me and my players got so caught up in Area that we practically skipped the whole 6000 years between--player section being explicitly without much info on Irem let's the ST introduce it naturally, and prevents &quot;I was a the if in irem, who became a tax collector&quot; mindsets, and puts them clearly in that foggy mindset of a mummy. &quot;I know I am Mesen Nebu, and believe it. What did I do in life? Don't remember&quot; should've been what popped into mind for my players. If the Wall is gonna be there, make even the core meatier with it. PC section as basically the same as a newborn vampire with amnesia, talk about skipping through time, faking your memories, all that. But move the history of iarea and guilds into ST only.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T04:48:38-07:00","id":854994,"title":"","content":"That's all pretty much what I interpret the game as now anyway.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of Guilds as archetypes a LOT, though, especially if high enough Memory unveils the curtain behind those archetypes as the 'jobs' they had as mortals. Then again, it is sort of what Guilds are already, or at least it doesn't have to change that much for said interpretation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T05:21:58-07:00","id":855003,"title":"","content":"Exactly. By now, when Mummy st's have read it all, its actually rather simply and brilliantly laid out. Like in Dreams of Avarice, remembering exactly WHY your Mummy was in the guild in his mortal life should be endgame stuff, not even accessible by Flashback beyond maybe &quot;Oh hey, i remember her&quot;, and even then, who knows if you met her recently. Part of me wishes they put the whole idea of what mummies are like now from Guildhalls in the core, and kept the actual Iremite history in the ST section. Let the players figure out why their mummy is rich and sassy and maims their high priest's hot son. Not only don't reveal what each Mummy did as a living person, don't even reveal what each GUILD did. Present them as weird lovecraftian societies calling on reeeeeally dark magic, without the context beyond the vaguest sense. So that players who think Mummy won't be like &quot;I was a potter in my first life, what guild would that be?&quot;. Make it NOW. Wanna play sexy vampire? Daeva. Wanna play a sexy rich Mummy? Mesen-Nebu. Wanna be the Mummy who demands that people obey the old ways? Maa-kep. Are you a necromantic horror who can almost remember secrets that time forgot? Su-menent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":935,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","user":"Cleverest of Things","date":".  sorry, somehow my phone and this forum have a disturbing idea of autocorrect 03-29-2016, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T05:36:36-07:00","id":855007,"title":"","content":"Many apologies to double post, but I realized something. If we have things like quick starts, previews, and other shortened books.. what if the Player's section was short and cheap. Bare bones. Aimed at making a starting mummy. Not as thorough as starting a vampire, but not quite as railroaded as an SAS or quick starter. Make the player mummy fairly... eh... thin, bare bones, heh. Basic rules and what it feels like to be a recently risen memory 3 mummy. How to pick vague memories of your past life. How to create an ancient preserved corpse via character stats, and then dive into who they used to be. How to get into the mind of the mummy. But take out all the rest. Make a thin, cheap Player book, something people won't be ashamed to pick up. And subsequently make a thicker, more useful storyteller version. Cost differences could help. Players might pick up a 10 dollar Mummy Player Starter book, and look for storytellers who want the 40 or 50 dollar ST guide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T12:07:05-07:00","id":855167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=855007#post855007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many apologies to double post, but I realized something. If we have things like quick starts, previews, and other shortened books.. what if the Player's section was short and cheap. Bare bones. Aimed at making a starting mummy. Not as thorough as starting a vampire, but not quite as railroaded as an SAS or quick starter. Make the player mummy fairly... eh... thin, bare bones, heh. Basic rules and what it feels like to be a recently risen memory 3 mummy. How to pick vague memories of your past life. How to create an ancient preserved corpse via character stats, and then dive into who they used to be. How to get into the mind of the mummy. But take out all the rest. Make a thin, cheap Player book, something people won't be ashamed to pick up. And subsequently make a thicker, more useful storyteller version. Cost differences could help. Players might pick up a 10 dollar Mummy Player Starter book, and look for storytellers who want the 40 or 50 dollar ST guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean like they did with 1e?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T17:24:39-07:00","id":855370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=855167#post855167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean like they did with 1e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this. Personally, I like the way this was done in 1E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T17:42:55-07:00","id":855383,"title":"","content":"Slightly off-topic, but I was looking at the <i>Ruins of Empire</i> recently and I've become even more convinced that they need to do a setting blurb for San Jose/Silicon Valley. They actually mention <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harvey_Spencer_Lewis\" target=\"_blank\">Harvey Spencer Lewis</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_Mystical_Order_Rosae_Crucis\" target=\"_blank\">AMORC</a> (The Ancient Mystical Order Ros\u00e6 Crucis) as possible antagonists/frienemies for the period. They mention that the Order, despite seemingly having no real inkling about Irem, the Arisen, or Sekhem, acquire numerous relics and vestiges (not to mention other artifacts that may be of interest to Arisen for one reason or another) during and after Lewis funds an expedition to Tel el Amarna. For the most part, these wind up at the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosicrucian_Egyptian_Museum\" target=\"_blank\">Rosicrucian Egyptian Museum</a> in San Jose.<br /> <br /> Rosicrucian park itself could make a great base for a cult, either Arisen or Deceived. It's got an Egyptian-style temple, a private research library, a planetarium, and even a reproduction of an Egyptian rock-cut tomb. It's also become a bit of a tourist trap, which could lead to some amusing difficulties for any of the Deathless who establish tombs there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T17:52:05-07:00","id":855391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=855167#post855167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean like they did with 1e?</div> </div> </div> </div>I pointed out the differences--move Iremite history and all guild history into the ST section, remove a lot of stuff a starter mummy won't know, thin it down until its extremely lean and even cheaper. Granted, I have the deluxe version, so I have no idea how cheap the player only section was. But iI'd rather the PC guide be more like a quick start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T07:19:17-07:00","id":855677,"title":"","content":"One potential solution would simply to keep all of the &quot;storyteller&quot; info out of the core book and save it for a STG. The space could be used to further develop cults, cultists and their roles, and to add additional systems for walking around with amnesia (more or less).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T07:23:47-07:00","id":855682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=854942#post854942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sothic Chronicles.<br /> Strix rock the boat of the Damned's carefully balanced politics. Idigam are the unknowable prey to the world's best hunters. The Fallen World is an endless mystery to the only people who see the truth. The Sothic Turn is a period where those who have the longest memories are blindsided by a world that's outgrown them and changed in ways they didn't expect; it's time to either get busy livin' or get busy dyin', and that's a whole lot said for Mummies</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be interesting if an Alchemist-like (see P:tC 2e in a few months) antagonist was added. Like some kind of archaeologist/cultist-type who plunder the Cursed's Relics.<br /> <br /> Regarding 2e, I wouldn't be sad if the &quot;find relic, feed relic to judges, rinse, repeat&quot; cycle was changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T06:27:35-07:00","id":858949,"title":"","content":"I really like Mummy and the concept of the death/reborn cycle. But the intercourse between death and reborn (5 or 6 months only) Is really too short! If the 2nd edition will come out, I hope they're going to extend it. Some years instead of some months, seems more reasonable to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T08:15:33-07:00","id":859014,"title":"","content":"There are a lot of weird ways to extend your Descent, but I realize now that my NPC mummies dont even last long enough to finish a full descent--they get into fights with enemies, they question the gods, shit hit the fans, and a descent roll robs them of months of life. Granted, as its a crossover game, and I dont have many PC mummies, the NPCs do sorta fill that role of loss--the others watch mummy friends decline, then suddenly die of circumstance. Sure, Ive run into the problem of trying to have mummies vaguely in the same historical period interact, but then the math shows they couldnt have (sothic turn 1, im looking at you, you nightmare of math).. but I still say thats working as intended, and that relic devouring is sorta like cannibalism in Werewolf. In 1e theres was almost no temptation to do it. In 2e, my werewolf npc literally HAD to do it (10 harmony, 0 essence), and i think relic devouring is the equivalent temptation. in a crossover game, at least, the story seems suited to having short lifespan. In a non-crossover game, the desperate desire to extend your life even a few more months also has a big place. Ongoing with the old age metaphors, you could picture a human cultist PC having moral issues over just what the Mummy is willing to undergo just to live a LITTLE bit longer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T09:41:00-07:00","id":859072,"title":"","content":"If you really need to be active longer, couldn't you just instruct your mortal cultists to wake up up again ASAP, with specific instructions for what First Purpose he wants to be assigned? You'd run into memory problems, of course, but that's sort of the price of doing business as a mummy. Based on the setting material I've read, I don't think this kind of thing is all that uncommon; as I recall, there are plenty of mentions of Arisen leaving instructions for their cults to awaken them so that they can be present for specific events or to enact some part of a long-term plan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T20:05:27-07:00","id":864065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=850272#post850272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2E wish: don't make me read between the lines across multiple books to understand the game. Keep a storyteller only section, fine, just actually use it to explain the premise rather than doing half of it and making me go hunting for the rest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like they've exhausted their list of shockers in that regard anyway. I mean, third edition basically spilled all the beans already. Not much more they can do. Unless it turns out A'aru is filled with terrible Cthulusque horror and the Arisen realize to their dismay that Ammut was a good guy trying to mercy kill existence to spare us all from the onslaught","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T20:14:26-07:00","id":864070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=864065#post864065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, <b>third edition</b> basically spilled all the beans already.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026Was there an autocorrect error in this sentence or have I missed something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T20:50:21-07:00","id":864082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=864070#post864070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026Was there an autocorrect error in this sentence or have I missed something?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oops. I guess my secret's out. I am indeed from the future! Man, looking back the relationship between Paradox and Onyx Path seemed so promising. Then the death sports began....Such a waste.<br /> <br /> Anyway! Yes, probably a typo or a stupid autocorrect. Should have been first edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T20:58:07-07:00","id":864087,"title":"","content":"I can think of one Chronicle that could be fun. The Irem Chronicle.<br /> <br /> You can see them. Subtle at first, slithering in the shadows of Neter-Khertet. You half remember them from your nightmares of Duat. Before the Judgment. The Slaughterers. The demons. But why are they HERE? In the waking world, the land of flesh, far from the mazes of Duat? How can that be? Unless...something let them slip through?<br /> <br /> Then the storms begin. Violent, preternatural, ripping unseen through the twilight, storms of sand and ghosts and boiling clouds. On the wind you can hear screams. And the roar of Ammut. Something is very wrong. Or very right.<br /> <br /> As the sands begin to quake and the pillars start to rise, you discern the truth. Something is calling Irem back. Forces on this side and the other are bringing the Nameless City back up from the depths of the deadlands. The Shan'iatu have returned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T21:50:51-07:00","id":864114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=864087#post864087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can think of one Chronicle that could be fun. The Irem Chronicle.<br /> <br /> You can see them. Subtle at first, slithering in the shadows of Neter-Khertet. You half remember them from your nightmares of Duat. Before the Judgment. The Slaughterers. The demons. But why are they HERE? In the waking world, the land of flesh, far from the mazes of Duat? How can that be? Unless...something let them slip through?<br /> <br /> Then the storms begin. Violent, preternatural, ripping unseen through the twilight, storms of sand and ghosts and boiling clouds. On the wind you can hear screams. And the roar of Ammut. Something is very wrong. Or very right.<br /> <br /> As the sands begin to quake and the pillars start to rise, you discern the truth. Something is calling Irem back. Forces on this side and the other are bringing the Nameless City back up from the depths of the deadlands. The Shan'iatu have returned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a single 2e has changed the setting like this. Why start now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T08:29:03-07:00","id":864310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=864114#post864114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not a single 2e has changed the setting like this. Why start now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh look. Atamajakki dismissed an entire concept out of hand. It must be Tuesday.<br /> <br /> I do apologize, though. That last paragraph may have confused you. Let me clarify. The concept behind the Chronicle isn't about Irem returning per se. Its about the threat (or as some Mummies would view it, the hope) that it would return. The Shan'iatu are certainly desperate to break free from Duat. Hounded and tormented as they are, they still have enough power to influence the mortal realm in small ways. So they call to their servants, those still willing to listen. They find unlikely allies in the Shuankhsen, for the Devourer has something to gain by Irem's return as well. The Chronicle is about the realization, through encounters with creatures from the deepest reaches of Duat and the restoration of Iremite ruins (one pillar at a time) that someone is calling Irem back to life, in the process causing the doorways into Duat to swing open and let out horrors from the dawn of time. The mummies will need to decide whether to listen to their Judges and put a stop to these groups or aid them in their efforts. <br /> <br /> If the vampires ignore the signs and do nothing, the Strix will continue to nest and multiply around their Havens until one night every vampire in the city is nothing but a host and plaything for them. If the werewolves ignore the signs and do nothing the idigam will warp the Shadow and the material world to suit their alien natures. This chronicle is no different in that regard- there is the threat of a significant game changer on the horizon, and the PCs have an opportunity to prevent it. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T04:30:17-07:00","id":864819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=864310#post864310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They find unlikely allies in the Shuankhsen, for the Devourer has something to gain by Irem's return as well...causing the doorways into Duat to swing open and let out horrors from the dawn of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's okay, I'll dismiss it out of hand, too, because that makes me like the idea less already. I don't think they would seek out Shuankhsen as allies. It'd be more in theme with the game, I think, for them to just act through the Arisen since they're their puppets anyway. Duat opening is cool...but the whole point is that it's like sealed off from the Mummies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=864310#post864310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the vampires ignore the signs and do nothing, the Strix will continue to nest and multiply around their Havens until one night every vampire in the city is nothing but a host and plaything for them. If the werewolves ignore the signs and do nothing the idigam will warp the Shadow and the material world to suit their alien natures. This chronicle is no different in that regard- there is the threat of a significant game changer on the horizon, and the PCs have an opportunity to prevent it.</div> </div> </div> </div>But yeah, I suppose I can't argue with that. I think it's a little more complicated than that, though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T08:58:41-07:00","id":864977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=864819#post864819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's okay, I'll dismiss it out of hand, too, because that makes me like the idea less already. I don't think they would seek out Shuankhsen as allies. It'd be more in theme with the game, I think, for them to just act through the Arisen since they're their puppets anyway. Duat opening is cool...but the whole point is that it's like sealed off from the Mummies.<br /> <br /> <br /> But yeah, I suppose I can't argue with that. I think it's a little more complicated than that, though</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;It's okay, I'll dismiss it out of hand, too, because that makes me like the idea less already.&quot;<br /> <br /> You say that, but you've already done more to elaborate on your objections and what could be done to improve the concept. I'm already finding your comment more helpful than the last one because of this.<br /> <br /> &quot;I don't think they would seek out Shuankhsen as allies. It'd be more in theme with the game, I think, for them to just act through the Arisen since they're their puppets anyway.&quot; <br /> <br /> First off, remember that the Shan'iatu and the Judges are no longer the same entity. One was birthed by the other, but developed their own goals and desires because of their time on Earth. I don't believe we have any evidence that they are in direct contact with the Arisen the way the Judges are (the exception of course being the Deceived, but the Temakhs are bound to the material plane anyway and don't have contact with their former brethren so far as we know). <br /> <br /> That being said you raise an interesting point. When I put forward the idea I assumed that the Judges would be against the return of Irem by default. But its occurring to me that this might not be true after all.<br /> Suffering breeds Sekhem, and Irem returning would almost certainly bring great suffering to the world. So...would they side with the Shan'iatu, or stand against them? Hmmm.<br /> <br /> &quot;Duat opening is cool...but the whole point is that it's like sealed off from the Mummies.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I understand what your saying here. I would argue that Mummies are more or less the only creatures left in existence who DO have access to the place.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But yeah, I suppose I can't argue with that. I think it's a little more complicated than that, though&quot; <br /> <br /> No doubt. For one thing the outright return of Irem is a high tier Chronicle concept, no argument there. Possibilities to make it less grand in scale and more localized could include attempts to summon a single pillar back from the Underworld, limit the timeframe that the gate(s) will be open, attempt to &quot;merely&quot; bring back one Shan'iatu, and so on. </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T22:15:36-07:00","id":865329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=864977#post864977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You say that, but you've already done more to elaborate on your objections and what could be done to improve the concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough lol<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=864977#post864977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, remember that the Shan'iatu and the Judges are no longer the same entity. One was birthed by the other, but developed their own goals and desires because of their time on Earth. I don't believe we have any evidence that they are in direct contact with the Arisen the way the Judges are (the exception of course being the Deceived, but the Temakhs are bound to the material plane anyway and don't have contact with their former brethren so far as we know).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a moot point. The personal horror of playing Mummies (any of them, really) is that you serve long gone, distant masters who only show the most miniscule hint of attention when they punish you. Whether the Judges or Shan'iatu become physically present or active to the degree you're proposing is, I think, very inappropriate to the game's themes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=864977#post864977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I understand what your saying here. I would argue that Mummies are more or less the only creatures left in existence who DO have access to the place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but their access is limited by being allowed to go there <i>only</i> in their death state and <i>never</i> remembering what occurs there unless they achieve Apotheosis. This ties in to what I just said above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=864977#post864977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No doubt. For one thing the outright return of Irem is a high tier Chronicle concept, no argument there. Possibilities to make it less grand in scale and more localized could include attempts to summon a single pillar back from the Underworld, limit the timeframe that the gate(s) will be open, attempt to &quot;merely&quot; bring back one Shan'iatu, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well in Cursed Necropolis: DC it does happen on a more local scale, with far-ranging possibilities that are explored, too. I don't think the idea would be a bad one for a campaign, but I think it'd be out of place for a 'Chronicle' for the 2e update.<br /> <br /> All the other Chronicles in 2e are things that disrupt status quo without setting off a cosmological bomb like the Shan'iatu being freed, Irem returning to the material plane, and the gates of Duat flooding open. Strix rock the delicate boat of politics Vampires must enforce to keep the beast under control; Werewolves are expert hunters but Idigam are something they've never hunted before; Mages investigate Mysteries and the Fallen World is full of them; Firestorms spur the Created to journey through their Pilgrimage.<br /> <br /> So, maybe to inspire you more, I think a better approach would be the opposite: the Judges become more distant, Duat is more distant. Do Mummies think they've achieved Apotheosis or are they surprised by how much they even miss the lash of a whip?<br /> <br /> Or, going back to my idea of the Sothic Chronicles, we should ask what disrupts Mummy society: the first Turn that's not only post-industrial but it's post-nuclear digital age. Mummies are ancient servants of forgotten myths. What rocks that kind of society better than a world who doesn't give a fuck?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T23:57:09-07:00","id":865351,"title":"","content":"I can't quote easily on mobile, so apologies for that.<br /> <br /> My beef with your proposed Irem Chronicle is that Mummy is, at its core, a game about clinging to the past. The Arisen fancy themselves the divine servants and heralds of the greatest civilization in history... when actually they're the stooges working for an empire that (while powerful) has been dead for five thousand years and completely forgotten. Their gods do not speak to them, their Judges only interact with them by punishing them in the abstract, they've lost the ability to create the Relics that formed the core of their Guilds, and are essentially doomed to spend the rest of eternity as amnesiac slaves going through the motions of something they barely remember but think is important. That the &quot;good ending&quot; of Mummy - Apotheosis - involves casting off the shackles of Irem's legacy and finally becoming a free agent with your identity intact is telling as to the core themes of the game; letting go of the distant past and learning to be yourself once again.<br /> <br /> Bringing back the Nameless Empire and giving the Judges or Shan'iatu more of an active role in the setting completely undermines all of that and instead turns it into a game about Egyptian-flavored superheroes fighting an evil empire of the dead... which is fine (I think the Forgotten Realms did exactly that with Netheril for Dungeons &amp; Dragons back in the day), but it sure as hell isn't Mummy. <br /> <br /> And for the record, reseru, I love your Sothic Chronicle idea. Making the Disciples of the Wheel and their special Cosmic Utterance core to the game might be a fun idea to entertain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T00:12:09-07:00","id":865356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=865351#post865351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bringing back the Nameless Empire and giving the Judges or Shan'iatu more of an active role in the setting completely undermines all of that and instead turns it into a game about Egyptian-flavored superheroes fighting an evil empire of the dead... which is fine (I think the Forgotten Realms did exactly that with Netheril for Dungeons &amp; Dragons back in the day), but it sure as hell isn't Mummy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it is <b>Mummy</b>, just not <b>Mummy the Curse</b>. It sounds more like <b>Mummy the Resurrection</b>, from the little I know of it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T18:55:44-07:00","id":866598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=865351#post865351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't quote easily on mobile, so apologies for that.<br /> <br /> My beef with your proposed Irem Chronicle is that Mummy is, at its core, a game about clinging to the past. The Arisen fancy themselves the divine servants and heralds of the greatest civilization in history... when actually they're the stooges working for an empire that (while powerful) has been dead for five thousand years and completely forgotten. Their gods do not speak to them, their Judges only interact with them by punishing them in the abstract, they've lost the ability to create the Relics that formed the core of their Guilds, and are essentially doomed to spend the rest of eternity as amnesiac slaves going through the motions of something they barely remember but think is important. That the &quot;good ending&quot; of Mummy - Apotheosis - involves casting off the shackles of Irem's legacy and finally becoming a free agent with your identity intact is telling as to the core themes of the game; letting go of the distant past and learning to be yourself once again.<br /> <br /> Bringing back the Nameless Empire and giving the Judges or Shan'iatu more of an active role in the setting completely undermines all of that and instead turns it into a game about Egyptian-flavored superheroes fighting an evil empire of the dead... which is fine (I think the Forgotten Realms did exactly that with Netheril for Dungeons &amp; Dragons back in the day), but it sure as hell isn't Mummy.<br /> <br /> And for the record, reseru, I love your Sothic Chronicle idea. Making the Disciples of the Wheel and their special Cosmic Utterance core to the game might be a fun idea to entertain.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How do I put this. I think you have some valid points with regard to your interpretation and I appreciate how closely you've examined the themes of the game. I just disagree with several of your conclusions. <br /> <br /> I think the lessons of the game are very much NOT that the past is invalid. If anything, I think the premise suggests that one should abandon blind faith in favor of truth and knowledge- accepting the past as it was rather than what one idealizes and wishes it had been. The game suggests that this pursuit is not easy. In fact, it suggests it can be quite lethal. Pursuing the past means violating ancient tombs and awakening the vengeful Arisen. It means calling down curses from buried artifacts and being driven mad by Sybaris. And of course, for the Arisen pursuing memory endangers and shortens their time on Earth. Like the roots of the Mummy horror story and the Cosmic Horror of HP Lovecraft, the game offers a theme that the past holds alien horrors waiting for the modern age to stumble upon them. But far from being invalid, I would say Irem remains extremely significant today despite being forgotten by the outside world. Cults great and small still pursue the agendas of the Judges (or use their knowledge for their own ends). Mummies still walk the Earth, carrying the old magic with them. Worse, the servants of the Devourer are still active upon the world, as are the rituals to create Amkhata. There's also unknown factors at play here- does the Sekhem no longer flow to Duat? Does the Devourer no longer taste the souls of those Judged unworthy? How about the nameless demons waiting for their Purpose as per the Dreams of Avarice? Or the other races and things from the dawn of time sprinkled throughout the line? The past isn't depicted so much as irrelevant as incredibly dangerous to the modern world. But unlike Lovecraft (but still in keeping with the Mummy horror story) knowledge of the old past isn't futile (though it can break the mind) but essential. Mummies, having lived in those times, are the best equipped to deal with the terrors from those eras (the Amkhata, for instance). <br /> <br /> I don't see the idea undermining the setting. I see it as an extension of already existing elements- from the Purpose the Judges assign to the threat of the Shuankhsen and Amkhata. Also, and apologies for scratching at this particular pet peeve, but could we lose the whole 'superhero' characterization? First off, the game as is has the characters battling Shuankhsen and Deceived already, and there are bound to be plenty of instances in which a mummy is called up to protect the cult or save someone or something important to his followers. Those are perfectly valid stories to tell (and indeed are much more the focus of other WOD games like Werewolf, Geist, Changeling, etc). Second, let's be frank- the WOD isn't about superheroes, its about horror. The grim dark secret is that those two genres overlap in several ways. Confronting the strange and bizarre with the intent to put an end to whatever its goals are and protect the victims of its depravity? Yep, common ground. The difference is that in horror you usually don't choose to fight your battles. Rather than being the hero that goes out and confronts evil, its the evil that comes to confront you. Your choice becomes whether to die or to survive- and survival means beating the thing that is hounding you. Mummies OFTEN find themselves squaring off against things without any choice, either because it entered their tombs and awoke them or because their cult called them to battle. Pitting your characters against some other horror is not the only way to tell a scary story, I'll give you that. But I submit it is neither an invalid approach to horror (I would argue it is very much a classic of the genre) or antithetical to the setting of Mummy: The Curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T05:05:20-07:00","id":867492,"title":"","content":"I think there's a big difference here. The game is about the past, rediscovering it and confronting it. There's a <i>gulf </i>between a Mummy unleashing an ancient demon in a sand-buried tomb and then saying the City of Pillars itself plops itself onto the earth as the gates of Duat flood open and the Shan'iatu openly bark orders at the Deathless.<br /> <br /> The first scenario is about how desperately the past tries to be relevant. *cough* one of the erm...Dark Eras for <b>Mummy</b> *ahem* is a little bit about how much just <i>used</i> to be around that just isn't in the modern day. The Deathless and relics are all anachronisms lost in a sea of people that don't <i>get</i> what the big deal is. The theme of Apotheosis is the Deathless beginning to wonder what the big deal is, too, because the powers that created them are distant, lost, imprisoned, or apathetic.<br /> <br /> The second scenario, that you're proposing, makes those powers relevant. Don't get me wrong, that can be a really cool campaign, and honestly it could be a cool effect that happens in my Sothic Chronicle proposal - Sothic turns are the crazy time periods where, quite literally, the stars are right. Still, the game now is about how the Deathless wonder why they bother and if the powers they serve care or, hell, even exist anymore. Your proposal is a giant fucking <i>Yes</i>, they do exist and <i>they're right fucking here on Youtube</i>. That's a stark contrast - not a bad one, but a very big one.<br /> <br /> So while admittedly interesting with its own themes and questions it raises, as the game is presented right now your proposal does seem out of theme","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T08:45:44-07:00","id":873787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=854942#post854942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sothic Chronicles</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm somewhat unconvinced that the Sothic cycle is the greatest enemy of the mummies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T09:11:34-07:00","id":873811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=873787#post873787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm somewhat unconvinced that the Sothic cycle is the greatest enemy of the mummies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Judge Chronicles\u2026 that doesn't sound right\u2026. Judgment Chronicles?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T09:14:44-07:00","id":873819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=873787#post873787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm somewhat unconvinced that the Sothic cycle is the greatest enemy of the mummies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither are the Fallen World or Fire Storms, yet they both work for their lines. While I personally prefer the Apothesis Chronicles, Sothic Chronicles work too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T18:19:30-07:00","id":874150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=873787#post873787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm somewhat unconvinced that the Sothic cycle is the greatest enemy of the mummies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, what Second Chances said.<br /> <br /> From what I understand the focus of the Chronicle isn't the greatest enemy so much as the instigator of conflict. The Sothic Turn fits well because it forces all Mummies, which includes the Arisen's greatest enemies, to wake up. It's a time when the stars are right and all kinds of exceptional magic happens, so that's another cause of the plot dominoes. Last but not least the passing of time and progress of mankind is a great enemy to anachronistic amnesiacs, and this is the first Turn that's not only post-industrial but post-nuclear.<br /> <br /> I don't think Slashers are a Hunter's greatest threat either but it's about what upsets the 'balance' of the splat's society and challenges individuals on a thematic level","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T18:42:01-07:00","id":874160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=873787#post873787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm somewhat unconvinced that the Sothic cycle is the greatest enemy of the mummies.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Fallen World isn't the greatest enemy of Mages, but that's still its Chronicle.<br /> <br /> Sothic Turns fit that branding for the Arisen because it's what shakes up their status quo. For an Arisen with a needy Cult, it's the only time they aren't beholden to the will of others and are free to wander and do as they please; for an Arisen with nothing to wake him, it's the only chance to escape the endless sleep of death for another thousand years. Mummy is a game largely about the shackles that bind its protagonists, and the Sothic Turns are the only time when most of those are loosened.<br /> <br /> I'd argue that the only Chronicles that make sense for Mummy would either be The Sothic Turn or Apotheosis. They shape the game far more than any particular bad guy or monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T20:17:26-07:00","id":874220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=874160#post874160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sothic Turns fit that branding for the Arisen because it's what shakes up their status quo.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is <i>the most predictable timeframe in which they arise.</i><br /> <br /> The Fallen World gets the Chronicle Title slot in Mage because of the curveballs it throws at that gameline's omni-investigative mystery-addicts, which I'm reasonably sure Neall knows seeing as he <i>wrote for the book</i>.<br /> <br /> The Sothic Turn does not start a story in any especially meaningful fashion that has a Plot Complication attached to it by nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T20:21:11-07:00","id":874224,"title":"","content":"I find it amusing that we're trying to pin the great cart upsetter on a time frame when the Law of Suffering and the Avarice of the Judges is <i>right over there</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T20:41:06-07:00","id":874234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=874224#post874224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it amusing that we're trying to pin the great cart upsetter on a time frame when the Law of Suffering and the Avarice of the Judges is <i>right over there</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose that's already in the title. The Law of Suffering is the Curse (or one of them). Mummy: the Curses? Honestly, I don't think it needs a default chronicle. There's so much to do in the 1E core - hunt monsters, find relics, keep your employees busy and effective, do what upper management says, try to escape the horrific cycles of capitalism. I just want cleaner rules that do a better job bringing to life a setting I really love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T21:19:12-07:00","id":874245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=874220#post874220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is <i>the most predictable timeframe in which they arise.</i><br /> <br /> The Fallen World gets the Chronicle Title slot in Mage because of the curveballs it throws at that gameline's omni-investigative mystery-addicts, which I'm reasonably sure Neall knows seeing as he <i>wrote for the book</i>.<br /> <br /> The Sothic Turn does not start a story in any especially meaningful fashion that has a Plot Complication attached to it by nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the Turn /is/ a curveball. Yes, you know it's coming... but that's an apocalyptic situation; there's a bit of fiction in Sothis Ascends where the priests know next year is the Turn and they are scared shitless. During a Turn - which there's been a grand total of four of them throughout the entire span of human history - the world is flooded with hundreds of confused demigods with nothing to do but whatever their withered hearts desire. Schemes that have been in motion for 1,500 years come to their culminations during this one short year.<br /> <br /> That's dynamic. That's terrifying. That's /anything/ but predictable. <br /> <br /> It's also when mummies are most likely to pursue Apotheosis, because no other purpose can get in their way. That's worth a lot of narrative heft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T21:55:46-07:00","id":874262,"title":"","content":"And IIRC, <b>Sothis Ascends</b> includes mention that a Sothic Turn isn't <i>just</i> a time when all of the Arisen\u2026 arise; it suggests that if you want to do strange things with time (such as having different eras interact with each other), the Sothic Turns provide a perfect justification for it. Heck, it even suggests the possibility of the <i>next</i> Sothic Turn getting involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T23:50:34-07:00","id":874307,"title":"","content":"atamajakki pretty much covered everything I would've said in response. Basically, the fourth Sothic Turn is a great umbrella that covers any other topic discussed as a Chronicle focus thus far:<ul><li><b>Antagonists</b>. Oh yeah. Our trusty heroes aren't the only Mummies to wake up. The Deceived do as well, and who's to say the Shuankhsen don't have unholy Affinities that let them wake up at Sekhem 10 to really get in on the fun?</li> <li><b>Unusual Magic</b>. If there's a ritual that will summon the returned City of Pillars to the earth then it's going to require completion during a Sothic turn. If there's a ritual to brute hack an undoing of the Rite then it's going to be during a Sothic turn. Plus time travel. And prophecies coming true. Or not.</li> <li><b>Apotheosis</b>. Not only do <i>all</i> Arisen wake up (a plot instigator itself) with no purpose, they also remain at Sekhem 1 indefinitely unless killed. There's no better time for seeking freedom than during their free swim.</li> </ul><br /> Also, let's muse on this. Picture the 1999 <i>The Mummy</i> film. Really think about it from the perspective of mortals - it's kinda bat shit insane: some corpse walking around eating people and flinging around Biblical plagues while worshiped by death cults that suddenly emerged from nowhere. That's all for <i>one Mummy</i>.<br /> <br /> A Sothic turn is <i>thousands</i> of them awakening.<br /> <br /> I remember when <b>Mummy</b> first came out we were all kinda questioning the effects of unease Sybaris and how, in a city with so many Mummies or during a Sothic turn, mortals could resist joining weird cults. So in the DC city-book we got some explanation of how vestiges dampen the effects, but I kinda regret this. In hindsight I see now that unease Sybaris being out of control during these situations <i>is the point</i>. In-universe people associate Mummies with ancient Egypt not only because they're actually from ancient Egypt but because <i>half</i> of the Sothic turns thus far took place during that time period.<br /> <br /> In a thousand years people in-universe will look back at the 21st century and be stupefied by a resurgence of occult interest and apocalyptic cult movements. Geez, kinda sounds a little bit like that out of universe, too. It's a beautiful contrast between people turning away from religion but people growing ever anxious about the end of all things, one way or another.<br /> <br /> Sybaris is literally a Sickness. A Sothic turn isn't just a challenge for the Deathless, but it's a plague on the whole world.<br /> <br /> Say I have a poor imagination but I legitimately can't think of a better Chronicle focus for <b>Mummy</b>. Anything else would either be weaker than the other games' Chronicles or just fall under the insanity of a Sothic turn anyway","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T01:44:35-07:00","id":874350,"title":"","content":"Man, I was originally more interested in the idea of an Apotheosis Chronicle. A part of me still is, changing the setting for Apotheosis to be a bit more widespread, so that there was a justification for any Nome to have 1-2 free Mummies would make Apotheosis something more integral to the setting rather than something you would necessarily have to structure an entire campaign around. But you guys are selling the ever-living <i>hell</i> out of a Sothic Chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T00:31:15-07:00","id":878565,"title":"","content":"Some things to consider with the Sothic Turn<br /> <br /> - Do we still want it anchored in 2012, or is that aging the setting too fast?<br /> <br /> - If it does move forward, what changes have to be made to the previous three Turns?<br /> <br /> - On a related note, do we want to make the cycle more accurate? The Egyptians calculated the Sothic Cycle at 1461 years because they were counting exactly 365 days in a year. It actually takes 1460 orbits of the earth around the sun for Sirius to return to the same place in the sky, and the calendar we use accounts for how a year is technically longer than 365 days. So, even if we leave the Fourth Turn starting in 2012, we still need to move the Third Turn up one year, the Second Turn up two years, the First Turn up three years, and the fall of Irem up four years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T04:57:44-07:00","id":878664,"title":"","content":"I think it's alright where it's at. I don't see how it's aging the setting when it was four years ago","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T04:15:16-07:00","id":889005,"title":"","content":"The interesting thing about making the latest Sothic Turn the default &quot;setting&quot; of Mummy 2e is that it messes with the game's default story structure - ironically, by making it more in line with other CofD games, as the task-based race against time takes the back seat (somewhat) while the &quot;secret society of the Arisen&quot; gets more time to shine. There's finally time for Guild politics, messing with old foes, touching base with old friends, making some life-changing decisions like relocating your tomb or restructuring your cult (or perhaps building one from scratch, if one was unfortunate to have lost theirs to the ravages of time). The race against time aspect is still present, obviously, but with no specific goal attached to the Descent, how much an issue that becomes will vary wildly from mummy to mummy.<br /> <br /> Personally, I like this idea - the more typical game as presented by 1e feels a bit too focused for my tastes - though I can see some people feeling differently, as the &quot;life cycle&quot; of mummies and the sense of urgency it brings are the big things that set MtC apart from other CofD lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T13:41:04-07:00","id":891345,"title":"","content":"You know what might be fun? Setting 2E in a fifth Sothic Turn. Book of the Deceived already referenced Mummies in the far future: <br /> &quot;Some future epoch may see lonely Restless Stars rise upon the burning sands of Mars, staring up at the red giant filling most of the sky as they struggle to hold onto fading recollections of Earth like worn tombstones scoured of epitaphs.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T01:00:13-07:00","id":891616,"title":"","content":"While it could make for an interesting chronicle, it's definitely not something I'd like to see as the <i>default</i> setting for 2e. CofD is a <i>modern</i> horror game by default, and this instant familiarity with the setting and exploration of our own world seen from the perspective of various monsters is a large part of its appeal.<br /> <br /> As a supplement, though? I'd be all over that shit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T01:11:31-07:00","id":891619,"title":"","content":"You know... with each 2e book having multiple cities and settings.. it'd be fun to see the same city in two different eras for two settings, in addition to Tokyo and the others. Just to show how much a given Nome changes over time in a non setting book concise fashion. I'd also love a Bleeding Edge 5th turn and an Infinite Macabre turn 6.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T07:56:31-07:00","id":891729,"title":"","content":"Here's another idea: the Pyramid Chronicle. Release 2E in 3 core books (kind of like D&amp;D does). <br /> <br /> <b>Book of the Arisen</b>: Contains everything that a newly Arisen would know, including basic rules, affinities, guilds, Utterances, and how to direct Cults. Chapters are arranged in order of rising Memory. <br /> <b>Book of the Scorpion</b>: Contains everything that a player would need to be a member of a scorpion cult, including sample Mystery Cult Initiation status, sorcery and ritual systems, and Sadikh creation systems<br /> <b>Book of Judgement</b>: Contains the secrets of the setting along with rules for creating vestiges, vessels, Shuankhsen, Deceived, and Amkhata.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T08:17:15-07:00","id":891742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=850424#post850424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that it's a thread about second edition <b>Mummy</b> I don't see how saying that we want the game's setting information consolidated is out of place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Especially in a game that draws specific attention to dinstinguish itself by having secret history unknowne to the players and having a separate storyteller's section.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=850873#post850873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One minor thing worth noting; while Cairo is fun and the first place to spring to mind when one thinks of Egypt, I would love to cover Alexandria for both being slightly less overdone and also hosting some of the fiercest fighting in the Anglo-Egyptian War during the 1880s.<br /> <br /> Unrelated topic, but what would you all want from a Tokyo setting for Mummy? I imagine the local Arisen community is very small and largely recently arrived, and the regional powers probably don't want them meddling in the area.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alexandria has the Library, but Cairo has the oldest still extand university in the world. And Giza. I think it wins.<br /> <br /> While hardcore Buddhist monks who've essentially mummified themselves are more often associated with the Himalayas, Japan has them too. So Tokyo could seed the notion of other mummies - be they Lifeless, Twice Risen, something outside the Arisen's categories, or a myth - without going any further into the subject. Otherwise... what reseru said; the city hasn't been good to them. While full-on kaiju are excessive, the city might play host to an unusually large collection of amkhata.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=854942#post854942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sothic Chronicles.<br /> <br /> Supernatural occurrences are typical in any age, but the Sothic Turns are like a flood compared to a high tide. For beings that literally predate history, how does this fourth Turning challenge them in ways new and unexpected? In an era more socially and technologically connected than ever, when mortals connect to those on the other side of the world, threats are everywhere. For the Arisen it's a time of loss as man turns his back on traditional mysticism, but for their enemies it's a time of <i>more</i>: the Shuankhsen feed <i>more</i>, the Deceived re-unite with each other <i>more</i>, amkhata pierce the veil <i>more</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the things I like about Mummy is that it plays down immortal future shock, in that mummies are used to waking up to find the whole world has changed in them, and by now are fairly good at dealing with it. The extreme level of change in the modern world can play this up or down - and it can parallel the modern world with Irem - the Arisen are, after all, from a place with rapidly developing new technologies, revolutionary communications, and concepts now commonplace that didn't exist a couple of centuries before - so the modern world could feel oddly like home.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I'd go for a deep time chronicle, with flashbacks, forgetfulness, cults changing between awakenings for better or worse, long-term plans and adversaries, and the endless question of how relevant the Arisen's missions are the world that now exists.<br /> <br /> Oh, and this:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/849461-chronicles-of-darkness-mummy?p=874262#post874262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And IIRC, <b>Sothis Ascends</b> includes mention that a Sothic Turn isn't <i>just</i> a time when all of the Arisen\u2026 arise; it suggests that if you want to do strange things with time (such as having different eras interact with each other), the Sothic Turns provide a perfect justification for it. Heck, it even suggests the possibility of the <i>next</i> Sothic Turn getting involved.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Two mechanical changes I think I'd favour...<br /> <br /> Add a new reason for awakening: a crime within the purview of the PC's Judge taking place within a certain radius.<br /> <br /> Replace meditation for refilling pillars with something more active. The mummy has to act (and succeed) in a way that fulfils the purpose of that part of her soul.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}